Definition: Given any groups G and H such that H < G (H is a subgroup of G), and any x ∈G, we define the left coset xH to be
xH = {g ∈G : g = xh, h ∈H}
Likewise for the right coset Hx = {g ∈G : g = hx, h ∈H}.

Definition: We denote
G/H := {set of all left cosets of H in G}
Likewise, we denote
H\G = {set of all right cosets of H in G}

